.TH HD-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "hd-manager" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-manager \- make and sign the jobs of the hyprdebian estate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-manager key
.br
.B hd-manager schedule upgrade
.IR host ...\ | \ all
.RB [ \-\-at
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-\-expires
.IR time ]
.br
.B hd-manager jobs
.RI [ host ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-manager
makes the jobs of the estate, signs them with the manager key and sends them
to the hyprdebian dashboard, see
.BR hd-dashboard (7).
The dashboard hands them out to the agents of
.BR hd-agent (8),
which run a job only when it is signed by one of their
.BR manager_keys .
.PP
Run it as your own user, never as root: the manager key is a
passphrase-protected Ed25519 key in
.IR ~/.ssh .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B key
Make the manager key with
.B ssh-keygen \-t ed25519
when there is none, which asks for its passphrase, and print its public key.
Put that in
.B manager_keys
of the key
.B hd-agent
on the managed systems and of the key
.B hd-dashboard
on the dashboard, in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json .
.TP
.BI "schedule upgrade " host ...
Make a job for each host, sign them all with one passphrase prompt, and send
them to the dashboard.
With
.BR all ,
every host whose last report is from
.BR hd-agent ;
the systems that still run
.B hd-report
are left out.
A host that the dashboard does not know or that still runs
.B hd-report
is refused.
.RS
.PP
The sequence numbers are the next above both the highest the dashboard has
seen and the highest this manager used, in
.IR ~/.local/state/hd-manager/sequence .
When the dashboard refuses them because another manager took them, the jobs
get new numbers and are signed again, up to 3 times.
.RE
.TP
.BI "jobs " \fR[\fIhost\fR]
List the jobs and their states, of all hosts or of one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-at " time"
When the job may run; the default is now.
.I time
is
.IR HH:MM ,
the next time the clock shows it, or a date with an optional time, such as
.IR "2026-11-19 03:00" ,
in local time.
.TP
.BI \-\-expires " time"
When the job expires if it has not run, as
.BR \-\-at ;
the default is 24 hours after the time it may run.
.SH SETTINGS
The settings are the key
.B hd-manager
of
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
see
.BR hd-config (7).
A setting that is missing has its default value, from
.IR /usr/share/hd-manager/defaults.json .
.TP
.B url
The URL of the dashboard, with
.B http://
or
.BR https:// .
The default is
.BR http://dash.rsq\-online.ddns.net/ .
.TP
.B key
The private manager key; the default is
.IR ~/.ssh/hd-manager .
.PP
For example, without sudo:
.PP
.RS
hd-config-update hd-manager '{"url": "http://dash.example/"}'
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The settings, in the key
.BR hd-manager .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-manager/defaults.json
The default settings.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/hd-manager
.TQ
.I ~/.ssh/hd-manager.pub
The manager key.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hd-manager/sequence
The highest sequence number this manager used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-dashboard (7),
.BR hd-agent (8),
.BR hd-config-update (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
